rules.description:
Your rules, as a JSON object. The only required key is roles.liste: an ORDERED list, FIRST MATCH WINS, most specific first. Each entry is {"role": "a_name", "si_un_de": [conditions]} and may also carry si_tout_de (all must match) and sauf_si (none may match). A condition names one field or one property, and one operation:
  {"champ": "nom_du_type", "contient": ["cta"]}
  {"propriete": "Mechanical.System Name", "commence_par": ["VEN_"]}
Fields: classe, predefined_type, object_type, nom_brut, classe_du_type, nom_du_type, predefined_type_du_type, element_type_du_type - the same ones read_ifc_overview shows under 'identite'. Operations, from widest to narrowest: contient (anywhere, even inside a word), mot_commence_par (at the start of a word), commence_par (start of the string), finit_par (end of the string), mot_entier (a whole word), egal (the whole string). Case and accents are ignored, and _ - . / are read as spaces. You may also pass dimensions, noms_de_systeme and debits_et_pertes; they are kept as given.
